# NotiLab Code Owners
# Each line is a file pattern followed by one or more owners.
# Order matters — the last matching pattern takes precedence.
#
# ─── WHAT THIS FILE CAN AND CANNOT DO ────────────────────────────────────────
# Read this before treating a CODEOWNERS entry as a security control.
#
# Every pattern below names @gmahota, who is also the author of essentially all
# of this code. That means CODEOWNERS currently provides:
#
#   CAN:    a routing signal — a PR touching a listed path is visibly flagged as
#           touching auth, schema, CI or AI surface area, and (with "Require
#           review from Code Owners" enabled) shows up in that owner's queue.
#   CANNOT: a second pair of eyes. GitHub does not request review from, or count
#           approval by, the PR author. A PR that @gmahota opens against
#           lib/admin-auth.ts satisfies its code-owner requirement with zero
#           additional review. Both defects this file was audited over arrived
#           exactly that way.
#
# So the patterns below are useful as *labels on blast radius*, and are worth
# keeping accurate for that reason. They are not a review gate, and nothing in
# docs/manager/quality/QUALITY_GATE.md should claim they are. Real second-review
# pressure needs either a second human owner or a branch-protection rule
# requiring an approving review from someone other than the author — a
# repository setting that does not live in this file.

# ─── Global default ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*                   @gmahota

# ─── Core infrastructure (CTO approval required) ────────────────────────────
next.config.ts      @gmahota
tsconfig.json       @gmahota
prisma/schema.prisma @gmahota
prisma/migrations/  @gmahota

# ─── Auth & Security (Security review required) ──────────────────────────────
lib/admin-auth.ts   @gmahota
app/api/admin/      @gmahota

# Every API route handler. Previously only app/api/admin/ and app/api/ai/ were
# named, so app/api/user/ — the IDOR family — matched nothing but the global `*`
# and carried no signal that it was security-relevant at all.
app/api/**/route.ts @gmahota

# Per-user data plane. Listed separately and last so it wins over the pattern
# above: these handlers read and write rows belonging to a specific end user, so
# any diff here is an authorization change whether or not it looks like one.
app/api/user/       @gmahota
app/api/growth/     @gmahota

# The quality gate's own enforcement code. A change here can only make the gate
# weaker or stronger, never neutral — treat any diff as a baseline change under
# docs/manager/quality/QUALITY_GATE.md § Baseline rule.
scripts/quality/    @gmahota

# ─── AI integrations ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
lib/ai-service.ts   @gmahota
app/api/ai/         @gmahota

# ─── Database layer ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
lib/prisma.ts       @gmahota
lib/*-service.ts    @gmahota

# ─── CI/CD & GitHub config ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
.github/            @gmahota

# ─── AI governance (Claude / Codex / Copilot) ────────────────────────────────
AGENTS.md                              @gmahota
CLAUDE.md                              @gmahota
.claude/                               @gmahota
docs/manager/quality/QUALITY_GATE.md @gmahota
